theorem three-names
  note        Three names obtained in one line and exhibited in one line.
  assume there are a, b, c ∈ ℕ with a + 2b + 3c = 6                    (H1)
  then there are a, b, c ∈ ℕ with 3c + 2b + a = 6

1.  a ∈ ℕ. b ∈ ℕ. c ∈ ℕ. a + 2b + 3c = 6.
    obtain a, b, c from H1

2.  3c + 2b + a = 6
    algebra, from 1

3.  There are a, b, c ∈ ℕ with 3c + 2b + a = 6.
    exhibit, from 2
